 # JSON utility
 
-Run `python cli.py` with JSON on stdin. The identity action returns its value unchanged.
+Run `python cli.py` with one JSON object on stdin; one JSON result is written to
+stdout. On a `ValueError` (including unknown actions) the CLI prints the error
+message to stderr, exits with code 2, and prints no traceback. Operations never
+mutate the input payload, even when they fail.
+
+Actions:
+
+- `identity`: `{"action":"identity","value":<any JSON value>}` returns the value
+  unchanged.
+- `check`: `{"action":"check","number":"4992 781-2"}` returns `true` when the
+  Luhn checksum of the number is divisible by ten. The number may contain up to
+  100 ASCII decimal digits, spaces and hyphens; spaces and hyphens are removed.
+  If no digit remains, it returns `false`.
+- `append`: `{"action":"append","number":"4992 781"}` returns the normalized
+  digits plus the unique Luhn check digit, e.g. `"49927816"`. Leading zeroes are
+  preserved. It raises `ValueError` (CLI exit 2, message on stderr) when no digit
+  remains after removing spaces and hyphens.
+
+Example:
+
+```console
+$ echo '{"action":"append","number":"4992 781"}' | python cli.py
+"49927816"
+$ echo '{"action":"check","number":"4992 781-6"}' | python cli.py
+true
+$ echo '{"action":"append","number":"- -"}' | python cli.py
+at least one digit is required
+$ echo ...; echo $?   # 2
+```
+
+Boundary semantics: an empty or separator-only `number` gives `check` false and
+`append` a `ValueError`; a single digit is valid for both. Unknown actions raise
+`ValueError`.
